<title>USA: Producers Entertainment sets acquisition.</title>
<headline>Producers Entertainment sets acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Producers Entertainment Group Ltd on Monday said it has agreed to acquire Grosso-Jacobson Entertainment's U.S. assets and 49 percent of its Canadian assets for about $8.0 million.</p>
<p>Grosso-Jacobson has produced more than 600 hours of television programming and is known for its prime-time series and made-for-television movies. It is currently producing &quot;The Big Easy&quot; television show for cable TV's USA Network and is in production for two made-for-television movies, &quot;Let Me Call You Sweetheart&quot; and &quot;Moonlight Becomes You&quot;.</p>
</text>
